{
  "dom_id": "step-q103077",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $H?$\n\nI. $H∨(G∧H)$\n\nII. $H∧(H∧G)$\n\nIII. $(G∧H)∨H$",
  "worked_solution": "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nH∨(H∧G)≡H.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $H.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H∨(G∧H) & ≡H∨(H∧G) \\\\  & ≡H.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II  is *not* logically equivalent to $H.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $H.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(G∧H)∨H & ≡H∨(G∧H) \\\\  & ≡H∨(H∧G) \\\\  & ≡H.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
